UID:O4-LFNCqhogYYlt3HMK1E
SUMMARY:Wheelhouse Wednesday
DTSTAMP:20260824T033958Z
DTSTART:20260826T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Offshore Wind Drinks – Houston\nHosted By National Wildlife Fed
	eration – Free event. Please sign up to attend\nFor nearly twenty years\, 
	Texas has led the nation in producing wind power. Texas now hosts nearly 2
	0\,000 active wind turbines—more than the next three states (Iowa\, Oklaho
	ma\, and California) combined! Offshore Wind presents a remarkable opportu
	nity for Texas to continue its role as a maritime industry and energy lead
	er. Enthusiastic support and advanced planning will ensure that Texas is r
	eady to advance responsible offshore wind development in the years to come
	. \nThe National Wildlife Federation invites you to join us for Offshore W
	ind Drinks on Wednesday\, August 26th\, at 6 pm CDT\, at the Houston Marit
	ime Center and Museum. \nCome mix and mingle while learning about this eme
	rging\, reliable energy option that is producing power and creating high-q
	uality jobs. \nWe hope you’ll join us! \nSign Up Here https://www.mobilize
	.us/nwf/event/996730/\n\nhttps://houstonmaritime.org/event/wheelhouse-wedn
	esday/\n\nFrom Houston Maritime Museum
URL:https://houstonmaritime.org/event/wheelhouse-wednesday/
LOCATION:Houston Maritime Center & Museum\, 2940 Riverby Rd\, Suite 200\, H
	ouston\, TX\, 77020\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-maritime-museum
CATEGORIES:Houston Maritime Museum
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
